B3 — QR payment lifecycle wiring
- New file: easy-locs-ea1eb0ed/src/lib/qr/qr-payment-reactions.ts
  exporting installQrPaymentReactions(). It listens for the QR
  lifecycle events under BOTH the canonical colon notation
  (qr:payment_initiated/completed/failed) AND the dot notation
  required by the FIX_PLAN spec (qr.payment.initiated/completed/
  failed), so wiring is deterministic regardless of which form an
  emitter uses. Per-event in-memory dedup (1500ms window keyed on
  transactionId/reference + event timestamp) prevents the dual
  registration from double-firing.
  Behavior:
    * initiated → telemetry breadcrumb via structuredLogger
    * completed → invalidates ["wallet-balance",
      "wallet-transactions","my-orders"] via the action query
      client and inserts a single success notification
      (payment.qr.completed)
    * failed    → logs error and inserts a high-priority error
      notification (payment.qr.failed)
  Returns the standard unsubscribe disposer.
